  "id": "retrolental-fibroplasia",
  "term": "retrolental fibroplasia",
  "definition": "Retrolental fibroplasia is an eye disorder in premature infants that has been linked to exposure to excessively high oxygen levels. It affects both retinas, causing abnormal blood vessel changes and swelling that can progress to retinal detachment and a fibrous mass behind the lens, with possible arrested eye growth and blindness.",
